{"kind":"stack","id":"s-foodchains","title":"Food chains: producers, predators and prey","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ef","foreground":"#1d3b1f","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Producer"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-d","content":"A living thing that makes its own food, using sunlight. Plants are producers."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which living thing is the producer in a food chain?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Grass","why":"Grass makes its own food from sunlight, so it is a producer.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Rabbit","why":"A rabbit eats plants, so it is a consumer, not a producer.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Fox","why":"A fox eats other animals, so it is a predator, not a producer.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"In the chain grass, then rabbit, then fox, which animal is the prey?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Rabbit","why":"Prey is the animal that gets eaten, and the rabbit is eaten by the fox.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Fox","why":"The fox is the predator, because it does the hunting and eating.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Grass","why":"Grass is eaten by the rabbit, but it is a plant, not an animal prey.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"A storm has flattened the grass in the field. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Count the rabbits","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Look for the fox","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You count fewer rabbits, because they have less grass to eat. Food chains depend on each other."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You find the fox hunting near the wood. It has fewer rabbits to catch this week."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Predator"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-d","content":"An animal that hunts and eats other animals. A fox is a predator."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which animal is a predator in this food chain: grass, then mouse, then owl?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Owl","why":"The owl hunts and eats the mouse, so it is the predator.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Mouse","why":"The mouse is eaten by the owl, so it is the prey.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Grass","why":"Grass is a producer that makes food, not a hunter.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What does the arrow in a food chain show?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The direction food moves","why":"Arrows point from the food to the living thing that eats it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The direction the animal runs","why":"Arrows show who eats whom, not which way an animal moves.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The animal that is bigger","why":"Arrows show feeding, not size, so a bigger animal is not marked.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which living thing is always at the start of a food chain?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"A producer","why":"Every food chain starts with a producer that makes its own food.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"A predator","why":"Predators eat other animals, so they come later in the chain.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"A decomposer","why":"Decomposers break down dead matter, so they are not at the start.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the food chains lesson"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You can now name producers, predators and prey in a food chain."}],"actions":[]}}
